Title: GRAILS — Beat 13: The Swap
Author: the operator
Draft date: 2026-03-08
---

= Beat 13: THE SWAP

INT. TOGG HILLS PANOPTICON — RECEPTION — EVENING

Togg's penthouse has been opened into a collector's showcase — glass cases under god-ray lighting, everything immaculate, everything a backdrop. Eight-figure items glowing under custom beams. TWO HUNDRED PEOPLE performing enthusiasm.

The room is loud in the way expensive rooms are loud — the sound of people who are very good at being seen.

ZACH moves through it in a sport coat, a lanyard that says APPRAISER, a demeanor of professional disinterest. He's been in rooms like this enough times to know how to disappear in one.

He has the padded case in a document bag.

Across the room: HYE-JIN, holding court near the bar. Six people in her orbit. She doesn't look at Zach. She doesn't need to.

INT. TOGG HILLS PANOPTICON — COLLECTION ROOM — EVENING

The inner room. Glass cases. Quieter. Two GUARDS at the entrance rotate every ninety minutes.

The real box is in the center case — sealed, lit, the crown jewel on display.

Zach works the room perimeter. Studying cases. Making notes on a clipboard. This is what appraisers do.

His phone vibrates once. Deja's signal: rotation started. Ninety-minute window open.

He moves to the center case. The keypad. He types the code Deja confirmed.

The case opens.

His hands are steady. They're always steady. Twenty years of handling things that can't be fumbled.

He sets the real box in the document bag. He places his forgery in the case. He closes it. He locks it.

Fifty-eight seconds.

He walks back into the main reception.

INT. TOGG HILLS PANOPTICON — RECEPTION — CONTINUOUS

Hye-Jin's group has migrated toward the center of the room. Natural drift. The guards are exactly where they're supposed to be.

Zach passes near Hye-Jin. He doesn't look at her.

From behind him, her voice, casual, aimed elsewhere:

HYE-JIN
(to her orbit)
—the thing about Fleer is the printing.
They were a bubblegum company.
They didn't know what they were making.

PERSON IN ORBIT
Is that why they're worth so much?

HYE-JIN
It's part of it. The other part is
that someone put it in a box and
kept it safe for forty years.

She finally looks at Zach, just for a moment. Just long enough.

He holds her gaze for half a second. Then walks on.

EXT. TOGG HILLS PANOPTICON — PARKING STRUCTURE — EVENING

Zach emerges into the cool air of the parking structure. He can see the event venue across the canyon — all the lights.

He finds Deja's car. Gets in.

She's already running the short positions on a laptop.

DEJA
(without looking up)
Clean?

ZACH
Clean.

She nods once. Types something.

DEJA
The box?

He hands her the document bag. She opens it. Looks at the real box. She doesn't touch it — she just looks at it, for a long beat.

DEJA (CONT'D)
(quietly)
It's beautiful.

ZACH
Yes.

They sit in the parking structure as the lights of the event burn across the canyon.

DEJA
Now we wait for Elizabeth to do her job.
